The Pitts S-2 Special Aircraft can enter flight without additional power but will remain airborne at slow speed until sufficient power is achieved and then enter flight with a maximum level flight speed of around M0.45. For maximum utility, the aircraft can operate with a broad range of engines giving good economic advantages compared with conventional aircraft. The S-2 can operate in a much lower cost operating environment compared with conventional fixed wing aircraft giving cost saving advantages to the operator.
